headings answers a heading selection with every match's file path, heading text, heading identifier, level, and the span of the content beneath it. The selection is one operand written <document>#<heading>, either half of which may be omitted: <document> alone selects every heading in that document, #<heading> selects that heading in every corpus member, and an absent operand selects every heading in the corpus. A document half holding a path separator or ending in .md is read as a repository-relative path, and otherwise as a slug. A heading is matched on its identifier, so letter case and punctuation do not decide a match, and a matched heading is returned with every heading nested inside its section. Given --emit, the content each match stands over is written as itself instead.

Usage:
  spec headings [<document>#<heading>] [flags]

Flags:
      --emit   write the content each matched heading stands over, instead of the matches
  -h, --help   help for headings
      --json   write the matches as JSON instead of YAML

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to the repository's specs.toml (default "specs.toml")
